//? Title: Tournament selection: actual contestant draws and first-tie winners
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Tournament size changes selection pressure while depending only on fitness
ordering. Actual historical raw draws, contender comparisons and winner counts
retain the original200000-parent experiment.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Each parent slot draws k contenders with replacement and keeps the highest
finite fitness, retaining the first sampled contender on ties. Under ideal
independent uniform population draws and strictly increasing ranks0..m-1,
P(winner rank r)=((r+1)/m)^k-(r/m)^k. The historical finite xorshift stream
reduced modulo m has modulo bias; these ideal probabilities are references, not
an exact generator certificate. Strictly increasing transformations preserve
comparisons; non-strict transformations can introduce ties and need not preserve
winners. Negative fitness needs no special normalization.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/tournament_selection_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <algorithm>
#include <cmath>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <numbers>
#include <random>
#include <string>
#include <vector>
#include <map>
#include <set>
#include <array>
#include <tuple>
#include <bit>
#include <datamunge/random/quality.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/tournament_selection.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::tournament_trace({-1, 3, 3}, 3, 3, 1);
    std::print("| actual parent slot | contender | raw word | candidate | best before | best after |\n| " "---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", s.pick, s.round,
                   s.raw_word, s.candidate, s.before, s.after);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Actual finite fitness-1,3,3");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual raw contestant draws",
                                     r.random_words));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual selected winners {}", r.indices));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/tournament_selection_tiny.svg");
}
